Puddings tend to split when you hit them, so if you keep hitting them, 
all the while taking great care never to kill them (wait a while until 
they get their hp back, use low-damage "weapons"), you can keep 
splitting them and create "new" ones for as long as you like. When 
you've filled a good portion of the level start killing them off, 
remembering to leave a few behind to split the next "harvest" from.
The point of this is that the "new" puddings leave corpses and items 
just like any other monster, so you've got yourself a potentially 
unlimited supply of sacrifices and items IF, and this is the important 
part, IF you can muster the incredible patience pudding farming takes.
I, for one, can get up to two, maybe THREE new puddings before I flip 
out and annihilate the lot. Needless to say you'll want to aim a bit 
higher than this for this tactic to actually pay off.

